 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "`src/tessel/debughelpers.py` defines three exceptions.\n\n**`UnexpectedUnicodeError`** (L17) subclasses `AssertionError` and `UnicodeError`. It's meant for better reporting of unexpected unicode or binary data. Nothing in `src/` raises it, so it's defined but currently unused.\n\n**`DebugFilesKeyError`** (L23) subclasses `KeyError` and `AssertionError`.\n- **Raised when:** code reads `request.files[key]` for a missing key, but the key does exist in `request.form`.\n- **How it gets there:** `attach_enctype_error_multidict` (L81) patches the `files` multidict's `__getitem__`.\n- **Hooked in at:** `Request._load_form_data` (`src/tessel/wrappers.py:202-210`), only in debug mode, when the mimetype isn't `multipart/form-data` and no files were parsed.\n- **Message:** explains that the form needs `enctype=\"multipart/form-data\"`, and lists the file names the browser sent instead.\n\n**`FormDataRoutingRedirect`** (L50) subclasses `AssertionError`.\n- **Raised by:** `Tessel.raise_routing_exception` (`src/tessel/app.py:584-586`).\n- **Raised when:** the app is in debug mode and routing issues a `RequestRedirect` that would make the browser drop the method or body. That means the status code is not 307/308 and the method is not GET, HEAD or OPTIONS.\n- **Message:** names the canonical URL, notes the trailing-slash case, and says it only happens in debug mode.\n\nIn every other case, `raise_routing_exception` re-raises the original routing exception.",
